#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:1
msgid "LLVM Admin Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:3
msgid "Grant Commit Access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:5
msgid "Frequency: Ongoing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:6 ../../../AdminTasks.md:35 ../../../AdminTasks.md:43
msgid "Permissions: Admin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:7
msgid ""
"Description: An admin should periodically review the list of commit access "
"requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:9
msgid ""
"This can be done by searching for issues in the llvm-project repository "
"which have the [`infra:commit-access-request` label]. Any user that meets "
"the [commit access requirements] should be added to the ['LLVM Committers' "
"team]. The admin should add a comment to the issue when an invite to join "
"the team has been sent and then close the issue when the invite has been "
"accepted. Admins should close issues after sending the invite and invite the "
"requestor to reopen if there are issues. If there are insufficient votes and "
"it has been over two weeks since the last update, admins may remove the "
"`infra:commit-access-request` label to take the request off the queue. To "
"reopen the request, someone with repository triage or write access must "
"reapply the label to get it back on the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:20
msgid "Commit Access Review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:22 ../../../AdminTasks.md:42
msgid "Frequency: Monthly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:23
msgid "Permissions: Triage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:24
msgid ""
"Description: The [Commit Access Review](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/"
"actions/workflows/commit-access-review.yml) github actions job runs once per "
"month and generates an artifact called 'triagers' which is a list of GitHub "
"users who no longer qualify for commit access due to limited activity over "
"the last 12 months."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:28
msgid ""
"When the job completes, an admin should download the triagers artifact and "
"create an issue asking everyone on the list if they still need commit "
"access. Here is an [example issue](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/"
"issues/131262). The issue should have the 'infra:commit-access' label and "
"should use the same description as the example issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:32
msgid "Removing Users from LLVM Committers team"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:34
msgid "Frequencey: Monthly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:36
msgid ""
"Description: Each month an admin should review any open issues with the "
"infra:commit-access label. For any issue that has been open for more than 4 "
"weeks, any user who has not responded on the ticket should be moved from the "
"LLVM Committers team to the LLVM Triagers team."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:40
msgid "Action Secret Rotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:44
msgid ""
"Description: Each month an admin should rotate the secrets that are used for "
"GitHub Actions workflows in the llvm-project repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AdminTasks.md:47
msgid ""
"The secrets are personal access tokens that are associated with the llvmbot "
"GitHub account. An admin should log in to the llvmbot account, re-generate "
"the personal access tokens and then copy the new values into the "
"corresponding secret in the llvm-project repo's settings."
msgstr ""
